  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 `RandomForest` passes n_estimators, criterion, max_samples, max_depth and n_jobs only; `random_state` is unset (global numpy stream). The v2 `randomForest` predictor pins `random_state=42` (`non_tunable_hyperparameters`; v2 fits are reproducible, 1.6.1 fits only through the global stream). With `random_state` equal to the integer the global numpy stream is seeded with, the forests are identical, also with `n_jobs=-1`.",
    "Default hyperparameters agree: 1.6.1 first grid point n_estimators=100, max_samples=0.2, max_depth=5, criterion=squared_error, n_jobs=-1 (grid max_depth 5/10/30); v2 declares n_estimators=100, max_samples=0.2, max_depth=5 (space 5..30), criterion=squared_error, n_jobs=-1. Only `random_state` differs (unset vs 42). The `defaults` variant runs the unmodified preset against 1.6.1 with its global stream seeded with 42.",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading the CSVs (hyperparameter `gene_list`, a missing gene raises); the v2 preset selects the same list with `scaledGeneExpression(gene_list=landmark_genes)`. The synthetic gene names are in no shipped list, so both sides get a pre-selected matrix and the selection itself is not compared here.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64. The forests nevertheless have the same structure, because sklearn casts the training matrix to float32 itself and the split order of random data does not change under a 1-ulp perturbation."
  ],
